# gate-rules: paths and prerequisites per command. Data only, no logic: the guard scripts read it
# (guard-common.sh gc_rule) and implement each named prerequisite. Design: D2 (onboard redo,
# kit-eval/reviews/jiraiya-onboard-redo-design-20261102.md, "The split").
#
# Format: one rule per line, `<command> <key> <value>`; the value is the rest of the line.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. A key appears once per command.
# Paths are relative to the repository root. Only the onboard entry is filled for now (D2, D3, D4).

# --- onboard (/v0-onboard, guard-onboard.sh) -----------------------------------------------------
onboard phase onboard
onboard feature onboarding
onboard state docs/agents-v0/onboarding/state.json
onboard artifact docs/agents-v0/onboarding/report.md
onboard template docs/agents-v0/onboarding/_report.template.md
# start: prerequisites (checked in this order), then the status it sets.
onboard start.requires git-work-tree kit-installed not-approved not-awaiting-approval
onboard start.status in_progress
onboard start.next Run discovery and write the onboarding docs (report.md and modules/).
# block: the status it sets, and the next step it records when the caller gives none.
onboard block.status blocked
onboard block.next Fix the blocker, then run /v0-onboard again; it resumes from the files on disk.
# ready (Design: D3): main session only, after discovery. Runs the baseline audit with --record (a red baseline
# is recorded, not refused), runs the onboarding docs check, then sets the status and the next step below.
onboard ready.requires in-progress
onboard ready.baseline docs/agents-v0/discovery/baseline-audit.txt
onboard ready.status awaiting_approval
onboard ready.next Sensei reviews the onboarding docs and runs, in his own terminal outside Cursor: sh .agents-v0/scripts/guard-common.sh approve onboard
# commit (Design: D4): main session only, after Sensei's approve. Needs onboard approved in the state AND his approval
# record (gc_approval_ok). Stages these paths (those that exist or are tracked; *.lock never), refuses when the index
# already holds another path, secret-scans the staged content, commits once and tags <commit.tag><n>. The pack paths
# are the folders activate-stack-pack.sh writes (.cursor/rules/org, .cursor/skills).
onboard commit.paths docs/agents-v0 README.md .cursor/rules/org .cursor/skills
onboard commit.message onboarding: onboard approved
onboard commit.tag onboard-v
# shown when onboard is already approved (start refuses) and after commit
onboard approved.next /v0-roadmap, /v0-intake, /v0-triage, or /v0-maintain
